## 6. Stages — Connecting External Storage

A stage is a named pointer to a location where files live — either cloud storage or Snowflake's internal storage.

### External stage (what we used)
Points to GCS/S3/Azure:
```sql
CREATE STAGE gcs_bronze_stage
    URL = 'gcs://skypulse-triptide/bronze/routes/'
    STORAGE_INTEGRATION = gcs_skypulse_integration
    FILE_FORMAT = (TYPE = 'JSON' STRIP_OUTER_ARRAY = TRUE);
```

### Internal stage
Snowflake manages the storage. Used for temporary file staging.

```sql
CREATE STAGE my_internal_stage;
PUT file://local_file.csv @my_internal_stage;
```

### List files in a stage
```sql
LIST @gcs_bronze_stage;
```

