## 8. Snowpipe — Continuous Ingestion

Snowpipe automatically loads new files as they arrive in a stage. No manual COPY INTO needed.

```sql
CREATE PIPE gcs_routes_pipe
    AUTO_INGEST = FALSE
AS
COPY INTO raw_flights FROM @gcs_bronze_stage
FILE_FORMAT = (TYPE = 'JSON' STRIP_OUTER_ARRAY = TRUE);
```

### AUTO_INGEST modes
**AUTO_INGEST = TRUE** — requires cloud event notifications (GCS Pub/Sub, S3 SQS). New file event triggers Snowpipe automatically. True serverless ingestion.

**AUTO_INGEST = FALSE** (what we used) — manually trigger via:
```sql
ALTER PIPE gcs_routes_pipe REFRESH;
```
Or call the Snowpipe REST API. Useful when cloud notifications aren't set up.

### How Snowpipe works under the hood
1. File arrives in GCS
2. Event notification fires (if AUTO_INGEST=TRUE) or manual trigger
3. Snowpipe picks up the file reference
4. Micro-batch loading — files processed within seconds to minutes
5. Exactly-once delivery — Snowpipe tracks which files have been loaded

### Snowpipe vs COPY INTO
| | Snowpipe | COPY INTO |
|---|---|---|
| Trigger | Automatic / event-driven | Manual / scheduled |
| Latency | Seconds to minutes | On-demand |
| Cost | Per-file compute cost | Warehouse compute |
| Use case | Continuous ingestion | Batch loading |

