## 11. Snowflake Cortex ML Functions

Beyond Cortex Analyst, Snowflake has built-in ML functions that run inside Snowflake's compute:

### Forecasting
```sql
SELECT * FROM TABLE(
    SNOWFLAKE.ML.FORECAST(
        INPUT_DATA => SYSTEM$REFERENCE('TABLE', 'hourly_route_summary'),
        SERIES_COLNAME => 'route_id',
        TIMESTAMP_COLNAME => 'date',
        TARGET_COLNAME => 'avg_price',
        CONFIG_OBJECT => {'prediction_interval': 0.95}
    )
);
```

### Anomaly detection
```sql
SELECT * FROM TABLE(
    SNOWFLAKE.ML.DETECT_ANOMALIES(
        INPUT_DATA => SYSTEM$REFERENCE('TABLE', 'hourly_route_summary'),
        SERIES_COLNAME => 'route_id',
        TIMESTAMP_COLNAME => 'date',
        TARGET_COLNAME => 'avg_price'
    )
);
```

### Classification and regression
Snowflake also supports training and deploying ML models directly in SQL — no Python environment needed.

