## 15. Snowflake Architecture — Key Differentiators

### Multi-cluster shared data
Multiple warehouses (teams, workloads) read the same data simultaneously without locking or contention. This is impossible in traditional databases where compute and storage are coupled.

### Micro-partitioning
Snowflake automatically divides tables into micro-partitions (~50-500MB each). Each micro-partition stores metadata (min/max values per column). Queries skip partitions that can't contain relevant data — called **partition pruning**.

```sql
-- This query only reads partitions where flight_date = '2026-07-22'
-- All other partitions are skipped automatically
SELECT * FROM raw_flights WHERE flight_date = '2026-07-22';
```

### Result caching
Query results are cached for 24 hours. If the same query runs again and the data hasn't changed, Snowflake returns the cached result instantly — zero warehouse credits used.

### Automatic clustering
For very large tables, you can define a clustering key. Snowflake continuously reorganizes micro-partitions to keep related data together, maintaining partition pruning efficiency as data grows.

```sql
ALTER TABLE fact_flight_prices CLUSTER BY (date, route_id);
```

